course: dictionary
lesson: 15184
title: Strong words: seared
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seared is a word about heat, but it can also be about feelings. Look at the words around it: pan, hot, sun, steak, mind. Those clues tell you what kind of seared is meant.
explain: «The chef seared the steak in a very hot pan.» Ask: what would fit here? A hot pan browns meat fast, so seared means cooked on the outside quickly with strong heat. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Seared can also describe a memory. «The story was seared into her mind for years.» Nothing is burning here. The clues are mind and for years, so seared shows the memory stayed strong and lasting.
fact: Seared means burnt or scorched on the surface by strong heat.
fact: In cooking, «seared» means the outside of meat or fish was cooked quickly in a very hot pan. «Pan-seared» is a cooking phrase.
fact: «Seared into my memory» means something is so strong that you will never forget it.
fact: «Seared» can also describe a sharp, burning pain.
exercise: «The chef seared the steak in a very hot pan.» What does seared mean here? | Cut into thin slices | *Cooked the outside quickly with strong heat | Cooled down slowly in the fridge | Washed clean with cold water
exercise: «The sun seared the dry grass until it turned brown.» What did the sun do to the grass? | Covered it with cool shade | Watered it and made it green | *Burnt its surface with strong heat | Made it grow taller
exercise: «The sad picture of the crash was seared into his memory.» What does seared into his memory suggest? | He wrote it down on paper | He forgot it by the next morning | *He would never forget it | He drew a picture of it
test: «The bright light seared her eyes.» What does seared show here? | A soft, gentle tickle | A quiet, calm feeling | A happy feeling of joy | *A sharp, burning pain
test: Which phrase means cooked quickly in a very hot pan? | Icy-cold | *Pan-seared | Slow-cooked | Half-frozen
exam: «The story was seared into her mind for years.» What does seared mean here? | Burnt into her memory, so it stayed strong and lasting | *Strong and lasting, hard to forget | Quickly forgotten by the next day | Very cold and wet
